        "Text": {
          "type": "cexolocstring",
          "value": {
            "0": "*A road-worn woman in a fern-green cloak nurses a small beer at the corner table. As you settle across from her she slides a scrap of paper over the wood, without once looking up* Cold on the West Road this season. Colder still for those who cannot read the signs. *On the scrap, in a careful hand:* DAOR TSEW EHT SEHCTAW YERG EHT"
          }
        }
      },
      {
